#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrScrieDrieContent.tsx:7
msgid "<0>SCRIE</0> and <1>DRIE</1> are NYC Rent Freeze programs that can protect eligible tenants from future rent increases."
msgstr ""

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrScrieDrieContent.tsx:13
msgid "<0>SCRIE</0> is for eligible older adults, while <1>DRIE</1> is for eligible people with disabilities. If you qualify, the program can freeze your rent and protect you from future increases."
msgstr ""

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrAskLandlordContent.tsx:41
msgid "<0>You don’t have to agree to a proposal on the spot.</0> If your landlord offers to resolve the issue, take time to understand what you’re agreeing to and consider getting advice before signing anything or giving up a claim."
msgstr ""

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrAskLandlordContent.tsx:49
msgid "<0>You don’t necessarily have to prove everything yourself.</0> Depending on the issue, the landlord may be required to provide records or explain how a rent was calculated. Don’t assume that the absence of records you personally have means there is no way to challenge the rent."
msgstr ""

